From 638f027cdf35e8923e60a93ab444af18a0b3ba5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Anthropic)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:33:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(phase-0): safe JSON.parse, stop deploying audit report,
 i18n parity, bump react-router-dom
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 0 (Immediate/Blocking) fixes from the audit & roadmap report, plus one
follow-up (parser test coverage). Re-verified against current `main` before
implementing — see PR description / commit body for the re-verification
notes and severity corrections found along the way.

B1 — Unsafe JSON.parse on localStorage('global_abbreviations')
- schedule.store.ts: wrap the parse in try/catch, fall back to {} on
  malformed data instead of throwing inside initFromStorage()'s useEffect
  (no ErrorBoundary sits above it, so this previously meant a permanent
  white screen on startup if the key was corrupted).
- Added schedule.store.initFromStorage.test.ts: 4 regression cases
  (missing key / valid JSON / malformed JSON / both localStorage keys
  malformed at once).

B12 — Internal audit report was being deployed to production
- Moved public/AUDIT_REPORT.{md,test.ts} -> docs/ (git mv, history kept).
  They were sitting in public/, so Vite copied them straight into dist/
  and they were reachable at tdytime.vercel.app/AUDIT_REPORT.md. Same
  test file was also being picked up twice by vitest (once from
  public/, once from the built dist/ dir).
- No vitest config changes needed — the test resolves its own path via
  import.meta.url, and vitest's default glob already covers docs/.

B4 — i18n key parity between vi.json / en.json
- Added the 3 missing error.parse* keys + a schedule.* namespace (3
  keys) to vi.json, translated to match the voice already used in the
  analogous live report.*/upload.errors.* keys.
- Added nav.completed to en.json.
- Added scripts/check-i18n-parity.mjs so this doesn't silently drift
  again (flattens both locale files, treats arrays as atomic leaves,
  diffs the key sets). Currently 421/421 keys, 0 missing either side.
- Note: traced actual usage and all 7 mismatched keys turned out to be
  dead/orphaned (the app actually uses report.*/upload.errors.* at
  runtime, which were already fully translated). Fixed for hygiene and
  future-proofing, but this was not a live user-facing bug.

B2 — react-router-dom security update
- Bumped react-router-dom 7.14.0 -> 7.18.2 (pulls in react-router
  7.18.2 as a matching transitive dependency). Resolves both CVEs in
  the vulnerable range (7.0.0-pre.0-7.14.1 for react-router-dom,
  6.0.0-7.18.1 for react-router) reported by `npm audit`.
- Added src/app/router.smoke.test.tsx: mounts the real hash router and
  navigates through all defined routes (/, /today, /week, /semester,
  /stats, /settings, /exam, /dev, plus an unknown path) to catch a
  library-level regression from the bump. Does not replace manual
  verification on a real device/browser (PWA install flow, iOS Safari)
  — that's still recommended before shipping.
- Did not touch other outdated/vulnerable deps (vite, workbox-build,
  undici, @babel/*, etc.) — out of scope for this change, tracked as a
  separate follow-up.

Follow-up — parser.ts test coverage (previously 0%)
- Added src/core/schedule/parser.test.ts (15 cases) using the existing
  public/mocks/scenario-{1,2}.html fixtures: metadata extraction,
  mixed LT/TH sessions in one cell, LT/TH auto-detection via the
  "-TH." suffix, an entirely empty week vs. the "zero weeks found"
  error path, id generation, cross-week aggregation, and all 3 parser
  error throws (including the two upload.errors.parse* keys touched by
  B4 above, so code and translations now have a shared regression net).

Verification (full suite re-run after all changes):
- tsc --noEmit: pass
- eslint: unchanged pre-existing baseline (62 errors/26 warnings,
  none introduced by this change; all newly touched .ts/.tsx files
  lint clean)
- vitest: 7 files / 79 tests, all passing
- vite build: pass; dist/ no longer contains AUDIT_REPORT.*
- npm audit: 0 react-router/react-router-dom advisories (was 2 high)
- node scripts/check-i18n-parity.mjs: 0 missing either side
